<h2 id="promotions">Step 6: Run price promotions</h2>
<p>Temporary discounts bring in new readers, reviews and visibility. If your ebook is enrolled in KDP Select, you can run <a href="https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/G201298240" target="_blank" rel="noopener">free book promotions</a> for up to five days in each 90-day term, or Kindle Countdown Deals. Free days work best for the first book in a series or when you have another book to sell. Announce promotions to your list and on promotion sites in your genre so the discount is actually seen.</p>

<h2 id="content">Step 7: Keep readers finding you</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Short video:</strong> book trailers and short clips work well on TikTok, Instagram and YouTube Shorts, especially for fiction. A <a href="/services/video-book-trailer-services">professional book trailer</a> starts from $350.</li>
  <li><strong>Useful content:</strong> for nonfiction, articles, talks and podcast interviews on your topic bring in readers who are already searching for help.</li>
  <li><strong>Communities:</strong> join genre groups and reader communities as a reader first. Constant self-promotion turns people off.</li>
  <li><strong>Local and niche media:</strong> local newspapers, radio, libraries, bookshops and industry newsletters often welcome stories from local or expert authors.</li>
</ul>

