<h2 id="mistakes">Book marketing mistakes to avoid</h2>
<ul class="bp-flags">
  <li><strong>Buying ads before fixing the listing.</strong> You pay for clicks that don’t convert.</li>
  <li><strong>Launching without reviews.</strong> Line up advance readers weeks ahead.</li>
  <li><strong>Buying reviews or using review swaps.</strong> It breaks Amazon’s rules and risks your account.</li>
  <li><strong>Only posting “buy my book”.</strong> Give readers a reason to follow you beyond the sales pitch.</li>
  <li><strong>Stopping after launch week.</strong> Most books sell steadily over months, not in one spike.</li>
  <li><strong>Paying for vague promises.</strong> Avoid any service that guarantees bestseller status without a clear plan.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="bottom-line">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Knowing how to market a self-published book is mostly about order: <strong>fix the listing, build a list you own, get honest early reviews, focus your launch, then grow with small, measured ads and promotions.</strong> Do the basics well and every dollar you spend later works harder.</p>
